/F2 12.0 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 613.00 Tm
(Abstract) Tj
/F1 11.0 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 592.00 Tm
(This paper introduces AnchorScore, a simple faithfulness metric for systems that answer) Tj
/F1 11.0 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 577.00 Tm
(questions from an uploaded document. We built a test set of 200 questions written over 12) Tj
/F1 11.0 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 562.00 Tm
(computer-science papers. When the system was required to answer from retrieved passages,) Tj
/F1 11.0 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 547.00 Tm
(faithfulness was 91 percent. When the same questions were answered with no document) Tj
/F1 11.0 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 532.00 Tm
(context, faithfulness fell to 54 percent. A chunk size of 800 tokens gave the best recall.) Tj
/F1 11.0 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 517.00 Tm
(Cutting chunks to 200 tokens lowered recall by 11 percentage points. Thirty-eight graduate) Tj
/F1 11.0 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 502.00 Tm
(students rated answer helpfulness at a mean of 4.2 out of 5. We recommend reporting) Tj
/F1 11.0 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 487.00 Tm
(AnchorScore beside accuracy whenever a system answers from uploaded files.) Tj
/F2 12.0 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 462.00 Tm
(1. Introduction) Tj
/F1 11.0 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 441.00 Tm
(Document assistants often sound confident even when the answer is not supported by the file) Tj
/F1 11.0 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 426.00 Tm
(the user uploaded. Accuracy against a gold label does not reveal that failure. AnchorScore) Tj
/F1 11.0 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 411.00 Tm
(checks whether each factual claim in an answer appears in the retrieved passages. A claim) Tj
/F1 11.0 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 396.00 Tm
(is anchored only when a human rater can point to a sentence in those passages that states) Tj
/F1 11.0 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 381.00 Tm
(the same fact. The score is the percentage of claims that are anchored.) Tj
/F1 11.0 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 363.00 Tm
(The study was run at Harborview Research Lab between March and June 2025. The only language) Tj
/F1 11.0 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 348.00 Tm
(in the corpus is English. The only domain is computer science. Those two limits are stated) Tj
/F1 11.0 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 333.00 Tm
(again in Section 5 so they are easy to find.) Tj
/F2 12.0 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 308.00 Tm
(2. Test collection) Tj
/F1 11.0 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 287.00 Tm
(Twelve papers were chosen from an internal reading list. None of them is a famous benchmark) Tj
/F1 11.0 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 272.00 Tm
(paper, so memorized model knowledge is a weak substitute for the file. Two annotators wrote) Tj
/F1 11.0 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 257.00 Tm
(200 questions. Each question has one short factual answer and a pointer to the supporting) Tj
/F1 11.0 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 242.00 Tm
(sentence. Disagreements were resolved by a third annotator. The question types are) Tj
/F1 11.0 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 227.00 Tm
(definition \(40\), numeric result \(70\), method detail \(50\), and limitation \(40\).) Tj
/F1 11.0 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 209.00 Tm
(The numeric subset is the hardest slice. It includes counts, percentages, and named) Tj
/F1 11.0 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 194.00 Tm
(thresholds such as the 800-token chunk size. A system that rounds 91 percent to about 90) Tj
/F1 11.0 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 179.00 Tm
(percent is marked unanchored on that claim.) Tj
/F2 12.0 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 154.00 Tm
(3. Method) Tj
/F1 11.0 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 133.00 Tm
(Passages are embedded with all-MiniLM-L6-v2, which produces 384-dimensional vectors. The) Tj
/F1 11.0 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 118.00 Tm
(index is a FAISS flat L2 index. At question time the retriever returns the top 4 passages.) Tj
/F1 11.0 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 103.00 Tm
(The generator may use only those passages. Overlap between adjacent chunks is 150) Tj
/F1 11.0 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 88.00 Tm
(characters when the chunk size is 1000 characters. That overlap setting is separate from) Tj
/F1 11.0 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 73.00 Tm
(the 800-token experiment in Section 4.) Tj
/F1 9 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 32 Tm
(Sample test paper  |  page 1 of 2) Tj
